<title>NEW ZEALAND: Foreigners hold 59.8 pct of NZ govt securities.</title>
<headline>Foreigners hold 59.8 pct of NZ govt securities.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The proportion of New Zealand government securities held by foreigners rose in June to 59.8 percent from 59.2 percent in May, the Reserve Bank of New Zealand said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>			  Jun 1997	   May 1997	  June 1996</p>
<p>Bills &amp; Bonds    Value   Pct(*)   Value   Pct(*)   Value  Pct(*)</p>
<p>T Bills	  3,050.8   48.4   3,323.6   54.5   3,249.9   49.0</p>
<p>Govet Bonds   11,795.0   63.7  11,166.5   60.8  11,121.9   55.2</p>
<p>Total Securities</p>
<p>		  14,845.8   59.8  14,490.1   59.2  14,371.8   53.7</p>
<p>Benchmark Bonds</p>
<p>07/97	     627.6    40.9     649.1   42.2     921.5   47.0</p>
<p>07/98	   1,009.5    41.2     966.3   39.5   1,571.1   64.2</p>
<p>02/00	   2,185.9    72.6   1,937.3   64.3   1,454.0   48.3</p>
<p>02/01	   1,609.2    64.4   1,498.6   62.4   1,024.3   64.0</p>
<p>03/02	   2,148.6    85.5   1,474.8   58.7   1,395.7   55.6</p>
<p>04/04	   1,695.0    55.7   2,124.7   69.8   1,895.0   62.3</p>
<p>11/06	   2,185.6    78.7   2,199.4   79.2   1,615.1   60.3</p>
<p>02/16	     333.6    56.3     316.3   58.5	36.6   18.3</p>
<p>(*) Percentages represent non-resident holdings as a percentage of total securities in the hands of the market, excluding Reserve Bank and Treasury holdings.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom (64 4) 473 4746</p>
